From: Emerald Tablet <emeraldtablet@local>
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: platform split (GAME_PLATFORM_IOS), mobile options, iOS app target
Purpose: Split generic Apple handling into GAME_PLATFORM_IOS (iPhone/iPad) vs
  GAME_PLATFORM_MACOSX, with optional shared GAME_PLATFORM_APPLE; add a minimal
  iOS platform backend, an iOS app target for device families 1 and 2, and turn
  off desktop-only components (updater, innoextract, curl, cpptrace, Tracy,
  video recording) for the mobile MVP. iOS builds no longer compile or link
  Cocoa/Carbon/ForceFeedback, desktop launch scripts, shell-based URL opening,
  passwd/home-directory lookup, or installer-extraction helpers.
Affected platforms: iOS (iPhone/iPad), macOS behavior unchanged.
Upstream status: Suitable to upstream after review. The detection order
  (iOS before generic APPLE) and per-platform options are the documented G2
  seam from the Apple implementation plan.
Tests: scripts/build-ios-sim.sh (wrapper) configures and builds the pinned
  engine for the iPhone Simulator SDK; scripts/audit-ios-app.sh checks
  architecture, SDK, deployment target, and frameworks. macOS G1 build must
  still pass with this patch applied (regression).
Reason: The upstream CMake treats every Apple target as macOS and links
  desktop frameworks; the engine cannot otherwise build for the iOS gate.

